### Research Intelligence API: example requests for all five versions.
### Works with the JetBrains HTTP client and the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### Start the server in dev mode first:  SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev mvn spring-boot:run
### Dev mode authenticates every request as the seeded user "user-001" (no Authorization header needed).
### In production (JWT mode) add:  Authorization: Bearer <token>

@host = http://localhost:8080
@workspace = workspace-001

### ------------------------------------------------------------------ shared endpoints (identical in v1-v5)

### List workspaces (the seeded dev user sees workspace-001 only; workspace-002 belongs to someone else)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/workspaces

### Create a workspace
POST {{host}}/api/v4/workspaces
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Climate Research", "description": "Papers on climate science" }

### Get a workspace / its documents
GET {{host}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspace}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v4/workspaces/{{workspace}}/documents

### Upload a document (PDF, .txt or .md). Returns 201 with processingStatus PROCESSING; it becomes READY
### only after Atlas has embedded every chunk. Poll GET /documents/{id}.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="workspaceId"

{{workspace}}
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="author"

Research Institute
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="publicationYear"

2024
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="documentType"

academic-paper
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="tags"

energy,nuclear
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="nuclear-energy.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Nuclear energy provides low-carbon baseload power. The AP1000 is a pressurized water reactor with passive safety systems.
--boundary--

### List documents (optionally scoped)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/documents?workspaceId={{workspace}}

### One document
GET {{host}}/api/v1/documents/document-REPLACE-ME

### Delete a document (409 while it is still PROCESSING)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/documents/document-REPLACE-ME

### Conversations
GET {{host}}/api/v1/conversations?workspaceId={{workspace}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/conversations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}", "title": "Nuclear energy" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/conversations/conversation-REPLACE-ME

###
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/conversations/conversation-REPLACE-ME

### ------------------------------------------------------------------ V1: vector search + cited answers

POST {{host}}/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "What are the main findings about nuclear energy?",
  "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}"
}

### V1 rejects settings it does not support (400 MALFORMED_REQUEST)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "q", "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}", "retrievalStrategy": "hybrid" }

### ------------------------------------------------------------------ V2: vector | text | hybrid ($rankFusion)

POST {{host}}/api/v2/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Find papers discussing reactor AP1000",
  "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}",
  "retrievalStrategy": "hybrid"
}

### Exact-term lexical search only
POST {{host}}/api/v2/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "AP1000", "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}", "retrievalStrategy": "text" }

### Semantic only, for comparison
POST {{host}}/api/v2/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "AP1000", "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}", "retrievalStrategy": "vector" }

### ------------------------------------------------------------------ V3: native $rerank

POST {{host}}/api/v3/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Compare the conclusions of these studies",
  "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}",
  "retrievalStrategy": "hybrid",
  "reranking": { "enabled": true, "candidateCount": 30, "finalResultCount": 5 }
}

### 400: finalResultCount cannot exceed candidateCount
POST {{host}}/api/v3/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "q",
  "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}",
  "reranking": { "enabled": true, "candidateCount": 5, "finalResultCount": 10 }
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------ V4: tenant scoping + metadata filters

### Filter values that exist in your workspaces
GET {{host}}/api/v4/retrieval/options

###
POST {{host}}/api/v4/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Find recent research about nuclear energy",
  "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}",
  "retrievalStrategy": "hybrid",
  "reranking": { "enabled": true, "candidateCount": 30, "finalResultCount": 5 },
  "filters": {
    "publicationYear": { "min": 2020, "max": 2026 },
    "documentTypes": ["academic-paper"],
    "tags": ["energy"]
  }
}

### workspaceId omitted: searches every workspace you belong to (never anyone else's)
POST {{host}}/api/v4/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Summarize my documents" }

### 403: workspace-002 belongs to another user (enforced in every version)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "q", "workspaceId": "workspace-002" }

### ------------------------------------------------------------------ V5: configuration, diagnostics, evaluation

### Supported retrieval configurations and whether their Atlas indexes are queryable
GET {{host}}/api/v5/retrieval/configurations

###
POST {{host}}/api/v5/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Compare the conclusions of these studies",
  "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}",
  "retrievalStrategy": "hybrid",
  "reranking": { "enabled": true, "candidateCount": 30, "finalResultCount": 5 },
  "filters": {},
  "optimization": {
    "embeddingConfiguration": "default",
    "quantization": "none",
    "diagnosticsEnabled": true
  }
}

### Start an offline evaluation (returns 202; runs in the background). Replace the ids with real ones.
POST {{host}}/api/v5/evaluations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "hybrid + rerank baseline",
  "workspaceId": "{{workspace}}",
  "retrievalStrategy": "hybrid",
  "reranking": { "enabled": true, "candidateCount": 30, "finalResultCount": 5 },
  "cases": [
    { "question": "What reactor designs use passive safety?", "expectedDocumentIds": ["document-REPLACE-ME"] },
    { "question": "AP1000 cooling", "expectedChunkIds": ["document-REPLACE-ME-chunk-0"] }
  ]
}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v5/evaluations

###
GET {{host}}/api/v5/evaluations/evaluation-REPLACE-ME
